ally expect many  people to know who this is the eternals  weren't that popular of comics and crow  is definitely an eternal's villain but  what's interesting here  is that we're essentially dealing with  another thanos  he's very very similar to the mad titan  crow has existed for over 25 000 years  he was one of the first  deviants created on earth by the  celestials now the celestials created  the eternals and the deviants  while the eternals are very attractive  and nearly immortal peacekeepers the  deviants are pretty much the opposite  although they do live for very long  periods of time but the deviants and the  eternals have gone to war with each  other for thousands and thousands of  years and  crow has led the deviant army against  the eternals  now there's some really important  backstory that you need to know about  crow before we get into athena's big  secret and before we get into neymor and  atlantis  as i mentioned before crow is not that  different than thanos now thanos was  born of two  eternals but he inherited the deviant  gene but much like  thanos crow is practically  indestructible and if he does manage to  actually get hurt he can heal himself on  command all he has to do is think about  healing himself and it happens  but another thing that makes crow  extremely dangerous is he can actually  shapeshift again just by thinking about  it he can warp the tissue on his body  and he can even alter his skeleton  and skull in minor ways he's actually  disguised himself as the devil plenty of  times in marvel comics  even growing horns out of his head now  this is very useful for him because as i  said he's immortal crow has figured out  a way to never die  at least not from old age or disease now  the other deviants don't have this power  and he keeps his power a secret from  them so every thousand years or so he'll  shapeshift to look like somebody  different and just claims that he's an  ancestor from crow and that's why he  looks like him crow h